<X(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to play tic-tac-toe as X. The game starts with all cells empty. The first move is mine. Let me think about the best strategy here. Since it's the opening move, I should aim to take the center, because that gives the most potential for creating lines. But wait, the center is (1,1). Let me check the legal actions. The available moves are all the cells. So I can choose any. But the center is a good position. Let me pick the center. So that would be X(1,1). That way, I can create multiple potential lines. Alternatively, maybe corner positions are also good. But the center is better for control. So I'll go with (1,1).\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nOkay, so I need to play tic-tac-toe as X. The game starts with all cells empty. The first move is mine. Let me think about the best strategy here. Since it's the opening move, I should aim to take the center, because that gives the most potential for creating lines. But wait, the center is (1,1). Let me check the legal actions. The available moves are all the cells. S