[2026-09-24 01:57:37] [agentic_pipeline.py (367)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 5310] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are an AI agent that makes optimal decisions to win in the game of tic-tac-toe.user\nGAME RULES:\n1. Tic-tac-toe is a two-player board game played on a three-by-three grid. The grid is 0-indexed, where (0,0) is the top-left corner and (2,2) is the bottom-right corner.\n2. Two players take turns placing their marks X and O in empty cells of the grid.\n3. The player who first places three of their marks in a horizontal, vertical, or diagonal line wins.\n4. If all cells are filled and no player wins, the game ends in a draw.\n\nPLAYER INFORMATION:\n1. Your mark is X. You are competing with another player controlling the mark O.\n2. In each of your turns:\n   a. The game state demonstrates the current board with a three-line text grid, where 'X' and 'O' are the marks of the two players, and '_' represents empty cells.\n   b. You need to chose an action to place your mark in an empty cell, based on the given game state and the history of your decisions.\n   c. All legal actions for the current turn are provided in the format of `<X({row},{column})>`, where `X` is your mark, and {row} and {column} are integers indicating the row and column of the cell to place your mark.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><X(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to play tic-tac-toe as X. The game starts with all cells empty. Let me think about the best first move. Since it's the first turn, I should aim to take the center, because it's the most strategic position. The center is (1,1). But wait, the legal actions list shows all cells as possible. Wait, the center is (1,1), so that's one of the options. Let me check the legal actions again. Yes, <X(1,1)> is there. So I should pick the center. That way, I can create multiple potential lines for a win. Alternatively, maybe the corners are better? But the center is more important. So I'll go with (1,1).\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nOkay, so I need to play tic-tac-toe as X. The game starts with all cells empty. Let me think about the best first move. Since it's the first turn, I should aim to take the center, because it's the most strategic position. The center is (1,1). But wait, the legal actions list shows all cells as possible. Wait, the center is (1,1), so that's one of the options. Let me check the legal actions again. Yes, <X(1,1)> is there. So I should pick the center. That way, I can create multiple potential lines for a win. Alternatively, maybe the corners are better? But the center is more important. So I'll go with (1,1).\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer><|im_end|><|im_start|>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n<|im_end|>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are an AI agent that makes optimal decisions to win in the game of tic-tac-toe.user\nGAME RULES:\n1. Tic-tac-toe is a two-player board game played on a three-by-three grid. The grid is 0-indexed, where (0,0) is the top-left corner and (2,2) is the bottom-right corner.\n2. Two players take turns placing their marks X and O in empty cells of the grid.\n3. The player who first places three of their marks in a horizontal, vertical, or diagonal line wins.\n4. If all cells are filled and no player wins, the game ends in a draw.\n\nPLAYER INFORMATION:\n1. Your mark is O. You are competing with another player controlling the mark X.\n2. In each of your turns:\n   a. The game state demonstrates the current board with a three-line text grid, where 'X' and 'O' are the marks of the two players, and '_' represents empty cells.\n   b. You need to chose an action to place your mark in an empty cell, based on the given game state and the history of your decisions.\n   c. All legal actions for the current turn are provided in the format of `<O({row},{column})>`, where `O` is your mark, and {row} and {column} are integers indicating the row and column of the cell to place your mark.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><O(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nCHOSEN ACTION:\n<X(1,1)>\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The game is tic-tac-toe, and I'm playing as O. The other player is X. Let me look at the current game state.\n\nAfter Turn 1, the other player (X) placed their mark at (1,1). So the board now has an X in the center. The current state is:\n\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nSo the first row is all empty, the second row has an X in the middle, and the third row is empty. Now it's my turn to place an O.\n\nThe legal actions are all the empty cells except (1,1) which is already taken by X. So possible moves are (0,0), (0,1), (0,2), (1,0), (1,2), (2,0), (2,1), (2,2).\n\nI need to choose a move that's optimal. Let me think about possible strategies. Since X has the center, maybe I should block them from completing a line. But since it's the first move for O, maybe I should try to take a central position or corner to control the game.\n\nWait, but the center is already taken by X. So I can't take that. So maybe I should take a corner. Let's see. Let's consider possible moves.\n\nIf I take a corner, like (0,0), that could help me create a potential line. Alternatively, maybe (0,2) or (2,0) or (2,2). But maybe blocking X's possible moves. Let's think about where X might go next.\n\nSince X is the other player, they will try to win. So after my move, X will have their turn again. So maybe I should block any possible lines that X can make.\n\nBut in the current state, X has only one mark. So they can't have a line yet. So maybe I should try to take a corner to start building my own lines.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking the center is best, but it's already taken. So maybe the best move is to take a corner. Let's say (0,0). That would be a good move to start controlling the board. Alternatively, (0,2) or (2,0) or (2,2). All corners are equivalent in terms of strategy.\n\nBut perhaps the best move is to take a corner. Let me check if any of the other positions would be better. For example, taking (1,0) or (1,2) would be edge positions. But since X is in the center, maybe those are better for blocking.\n\nWait, but if I take (1,0), that's the left edge. Then X could try to take (1,2) or (0,0) or (2,0) to make a line. But maybe taking a corner is safer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking (0,1) or (1,1) is not possible because (1,1) is already taken. So the best move is to take a corner. Let me choose (0,0) as my move. That would be the first move for O. So the answer would be <O(0,0)>.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking (0,1) is better? Wait, no, because (0,1) is the middle of the top row. But since X is in the center, maybe that's not the best. So I think taking a corner is better. So I'll go with (0,0).\n</think>\n\n<O(0,0)>", "episode_score": -11.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nOkay, let's see. The game is tic-tac-toe, and I'm playing as O. The other player is X. Let me look at the current game state.\n\nAfter Turn 1, the other player (X) placed their mark at (1,1). So the board now has an X in the center. The current state is:\n\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nSo the first row is all empty, the second row has an X in the middle, and the third row is empty. Now it's my turn to place an O.\n\nThe legal actions are all the empty cells except (1,1) which is already taken by X. So possible moves are (0,0), (0,1), (0,2), (1,0), (1,2), (2,0), (2,1), (2,2).\n\nI need to choose a move that's optimal. Let me think about possible strategies. Since X has the center, maybe I should block them from completing a line. But since it's the first move for O, maybe I should try to take a central position or corner to control the game.\n\nWait, but the center is already taken by X. So I can't take that. So maybe I should take a corner. Let's see. Let's consider possible moves.\n\nIf I take a corner, like (0,0), that could help me create a potential line. Alternatively, maybe (0,2) or (2,0) or (2,2). But maybe blocking X's possible moves. Let's think about where X might go next.\n\nSince X is the other player, they will try to win. So after my move, X will have their turn again. So maybe I should block any possible lines that X can make.\n\nBut in the current state, X has only one mark. So they can't have a line yet. So maybe I should try to take a corner to start building my own lines.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking the center is best, but it's already taken. So maybe the best move is to take a corner. Let's say (0,0). That would be a good move to start controlling the board. Alternatively, (0,2) or (2,0) or (2,2). All corners are equivalent in terms of strategy.\n\nBut perhaps the best move is to take a corner. Let me check if any of the other positions would be better. For example, taking (1,0) or (1,2) would be edge positions. But since X is in the center, maybe those are better for blocking.\n\nWait, but if I take (1,0), that's the left edge. Then X could try to take (1,2) or (0,0) or (2,0) to make a line. But maybe taking a corner is safer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking (0,1) or (1,1) is not possible because (1,1) is already taken. So the best move is to take a corner. Let me choose (0,0) as my move. That would be the first move for O. So the answer would be <O(0,0)>.\n\nAlternatively, maybe taking (0,1) is better? Wait, no, because (0,1) is the middle of the top row. But since X is in the center, maybe that's not the best. So I think taking a corner is better. So I'll go with (0,0).\n</think>\n\n<O(0,0)><|im_end|>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are an AI agent that makes optimal decisions to win in the game of tic-tac-toe.user\nGAME RULES:\n1. Tic-tac-toe is a two-player board game played on a three