[2026-09-24 02:15:25] [agentic_pipeline.py (169)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 5310] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are an AI agent that makes optimal decisions to win in the game of tic-tac-toe.user\nGAME RULES:\n1. Tic-tac-toe is a two-player board game played on a three-by-three grid. The grid is 0-indexed, where (0,0) is the top-left corner and (2,2) is the bottom-right corner.\n2. Two players take turns placing their marks X and O in empty cells of the grid.\n3. The player who first places three of their marks in a horizontal, vertical, or diagonal line wins.\n4. If all cells are filled and no player wins, the game ends in a draw.\n\nPLAYER INFORMATION:\n1. Your mark is O. You are competing with another player controlling the mark X.\n2. In each of your turns:\n   a. The game state demonstrates the current board with a three-line text grid, where 'X' and 'O' are the marks of the two players, and '_' represents empty cells.\n   b. You need to chose an action to place your mark in an empty cell, based on the given game state and the history of your decisions.\n   c. All legal actions for the current turn are provided in the format of `<O({row},{column})>`, where `O` is your mark, and {row} and {column} are integers indicating the row and column of the cell to place your mark.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><O(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nCHOSEN ACTION:\n<X(1,1)>\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The game is tic-tac-toe, and I'm playing as O. The other player just placed their mark at (1,1), which is the center. Now it's my turn. The current board state is:\n\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nSo the second row has an X in the middle. The empty cells are all the others. My goal is to block the opponent's potential wins and create my own opportunities.\n\nFirst, I need to check if there's any immediate threat. The opponent has an X in the center. If they continue to play, maybe they can form a line. But since it's my turn, I need to respond.\n\nLooking at the possible moves, the legal actions are all cells except (1,1) which is already taken. Let me think about possible strategies. The center is already occupied, so maybe I should block any possible lines the opponent can make. For example, if the opponent is trying to make a row, column, or diagonal.\n\nBut the opponent's last move was the center. Let's consider possible ways they could win. If they place another X in, say, (0,1) and (2,1), that would make a vertical line. But since it's my turn, I need to block that. Alternatively, if they complete a diagonal, but that would require two more moves. Maybe I should focus on blocking their possible next moves.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should try to create my own lines. Let's see. The current board has an X in the center. If I place an O in a corner, maybe that can help me set up for a win. For example, if I place O in (0,0), then if the opponent plays (0,1), I can block them. But maybe that's too far ahead.\n\nAlternatively, looking at the board, the second row is 